WEBVTT

00:41.291 --> 00:43.961
NO TAIL TO TELL

00:45.170 --> 00:46.255
What if…

00:49.508 --> 00:51.176
I don't want to be normal?

00:53.053 --> 00:53.929
What?

00:54.012 --> 00:56.473
If you're just going to erase my memory

00:57.391 --> 00:59.810
and be the only one
who remembers this moment,

01:00.852 --> 01:03.605
then I should be allowed to do
at least this much, right?

01:04.856 --> 01:06.191
What do you mean…

01:21.582 --> 01:23.834
What… do you think you're doing?

01:24.459 --> 01:26.712
Unlike you, I'm not good
at doing things half-heartedly.

01:26.795 --> 01:29.965
If I decide to do something,
I have to put all my heart into it.

01:30.048 --> 01:33.093
Wait. What do you mean?

01:34.052 --> 01:36.305
Let's date. For real.

01:37.514 --> 01:38.640
I'm serious.

01:42.561 --> 01:45.814
You're still wet behind the ears.
Where did you learn to do that?

01:46.481 --> 01:48.442
What do you think you're doing?

01:49.401 --> 01:50.819
Why are you so flustered?

01:51.570 --> 01:54.323
- Is there a problem?
- Of course there is.

01:54.406 --> 01:57.993
Once we go back to how we were,
we'll never see each other again.

01:58.076 --> 02:00.120
So you coming on so strong like this

02:01.246 --> 02:03.290
is overwhelming.

02:03.832 --> 02:06.043
Then you shouldn't have led me on.

02:06.126 --> 02:07.502
I'm just getting started.

02:09.254 --> 02:11.381
Why? Do you want to stop?

02:14.593 --> 02:16.428
When did I ever lead you on?

02:19.389 --> 02:23.185
Don't think about running,
and don't just dip your toes in.

02:28.940 --> 02:31.026
Let's do this right. You and I both.

02:33.654 --> 02:35.572
From now on, I'm done joking around.

02:45.707 --> 02:50.462
EPISODE 9
LOVE ATTACK

02:52.255 --> 02:53.256
That nine-tailed fox.

02:54.424 --> 02:56.426
She said she became human.

02:58.303 --> 02:59.763
What?

02:59.846 --> 03:03.100
She's just an ordinary human now.

03:04.810 --> 03:06.228
An ordinary human?

03:08.980 --> 03:10.524
An ordinary human.

03:13.735 --> 03:16.196
Then that fox

03:17.280 --> 03:19.032
has no power anymore,

03:19.866 --> 03:22.035
and there's no reason to be afraid of her.

03:26.581 --> 03:28.291
This just got interesting.

03:29.876 --> 03:31.628
What are you going to do?

03:31.712 --> 03:33.672
- About what?
- What do you think?

03:34.506 --> 03:37.509
Now that things are in our favor,
you're not going after that damn fox?

03:37.592 --> 03:38.510
Why should I?

03:39.803 --> 03:41.138
What?

03:41.221 --> 03:43.056
Whether I skin it or roast it,

03:43.140 --> 03:46.309
I won't get blood on my hands
unless there's something to gain.

03:47.602 --> 03:50.105
Wait, what does that…

03:51.440 --> 03:54.234
They say cultivated beasts have an orb.

03:54.860 --> 03:57.738
Dragons hold dragon orbs
to call the wind and rain.

03:57.821 --> 04:01.992
Nine-tailed foxes have fox beads
to perform their infinite tricks.

04:03.285 --> 04:06.121
But if that fox
really became an ordinary human,

04:06.747 --> 04:09.166
her bead must've already shattered
and vanished.

04:10.000 --> 04:12.210
So, I'm not interested anymore.

04:12.836 --> 04:15.172
But look at what we suffered

04:15.255 --> 04:17.591
because of that damn beast
that's not even human!

04:17.674 --> 04:21.094
We were hiding like rats,
cowering in fear!

04:21.762 --> 04:24.514
Am I the only one who feels like shit?

04:25.432 --> 04:27.225
You all do, don't you?

04:27.309 --> 04:29.352
Didn't I tell you before?

04:29.436 --> 04:31.980
A hunter doesn't hunt
because of a personal grudge.

04:33.607 --> 04:35.609
Damn you.

04:40.530 --> 04:41.698
Wait a second.

04:48.163 --> 04:50.165
Then who erased your memory?

05:00.926 --> 05:05.222
She's an ordinary human now.
How could she have erased your memories?

05:08.266 --> 05:11.102
What trick are you trying to pull?

05:13.230 --> 05:14.856
She's not the one

05:15.732 --> 05:17.359
who did it.

05:18.652 --> 05:19.778
Then who was it?

05:20.570 --> 05:23.198
I don't know if she was
a nine-tailed fox or what,

05:24.491 --> 05:26.409
but there was someone else there.

05:47.889 --> 05:49.558
Let's date. For real.

05:51.476 --> 05:52.602
I'm serious.

06:09.035 --> 06:10.537
This is driving me nuts.

06:11.705 --> 06:14.791
What's wrong with me?
I couldn't sleep at all.

06:17.377 --> 06:20.297
And why am I so thirsty?

06:21.381 --> 06:22.966
Gosh.

06:23.049 --> 06:26.136
I'm dying of thirst,
but it's too awkward to go out.

06:34.895 --> 06:37.314
What was I thinking yesterday?

06:37.397 --> 06:39.858
Unlike you, I'm not good
at doing things half-heartedly.

06:39.941 --> 06:42.903
If I decide to do something,
I have to put all my heart into it.

06:42.986 --> 06:44.863
Put all my heart into what?

06:44.946 --> 06:47.532
Then you shouldn't have led me on.

06:47.616 --> 06:49.117
I'm just getting started.

06:49.200 --> 06:51.536
What's wrong with me?

06:55.624 --> 06:57.375
I must've lost it.

07:07.260 --> 07:09.137
She's going to wake up soon.

07:10.138 --> 07:13.266
It's going to be so awkward.
How am I supposed to face her?

07:33.787 --> 07:35.747
Did he really leave?

07:51.012 --> 07:52.514
This is so awkward.

07:53.807 --> 07:55.934
He could've just played along.

07:56.017 --> 07:58.144
Why did he suddenly get so bold?

07:58.228 --> 07:59.980
I didn't expect him to just…

08:00.480 --> 08:02.148
It caught me off guard.

08:07.404 --> 08:08.822
Oh, crap.

08:24.796 --> 08:27.465
Hi, did you sleep well?

08:28.091 --> 08:29.342
Yeah.

08:30.260 --> 08:32.053
What are you doing?

08:32.721 --> 08:34.681
Oh, this…

08:40.770 --> 08:42.313
Nothing.

08:42.397 --> 08:45.066
I was just picking something up.

08:46.276 --> 08:47.527
I see.

08:52.323 --> 08:55.160
Leave or just stay. Make up your mind.

08:55.243 --> 08:58.079
Why do you keep going back and forth?
It's confusing.

08:58.621 --> 09:00.457
Oh, I forgot to give you this.

09:11.468 --> 09:12.927
I'm heading out to exercise.

09:14.095 --> 09:18.224
I might be late, and you could get hungry.

09:18.767 --> 09:22.020
You should use this
to buy yourself something to eat.

09:22.645 --> 09:23.813
Okay.

09:28.818 --> 09:31.613
But why are you suddenly
exercising at the crack of dawn?

09:31.696 --> 09:33.031
Well,

09:33.114 --> 09:34.741
I recently realized

09:35.325 --> 09:38.745
that my body's a total wreck right now.

09:39.746 --> 09:44.751
My balance is off,
and I don't have any stamina.

09:44.834 --> 09:45.835
I see.

09:51.800 --> 09:53.676
Okay, well…

09:55.011 --> 09:56.596
I'm off to work out.

09:58.640 --> 10:00.350
Oh, sure.

10:00.892 --> 10:03.019
- Okay.
- Yeah.

10:19.994 --> 10:21.037
Do you…

10:22.997 --> 10:24.124
want to come along?

10:25.291 --> 10:26.543
What?

10:35.301 --> 10:36.386
Si-yeol.

10:37.554 --> 10:38.930
The thing is…

10:42.058 --> 10:43.351
my memory came back.

10:45.436 --> 10:48.148
What are you people planning to do?

10:49.357 --> 10:52.569
You don't have to worry about your friend.

10:52.652 --> 10:56.281
I'm only interested in the fox bead.

10:57.198 --> 11:00.702
It's not like Si-yeol
will be in any real danger.

11:00.785 --> 11:02.412
I should just stay out of this.

11:02.495 --> 11:05.498
Then whatever happens isn't my fault.

11:11.880 --> 11:14.591
But what if they actually kill
that nine-tailed fox?

11:18.386 --> 11:22.307
Would Si-yeol
have to live my life forever?

11:22.849 --> 11:23.808
Gosh.

11:26.936 --> 11:28.605
Woo-seok.

11:28.688 --> 11:30.315
Dad.

11:32.025 --> 11:33.276
You feeling okay?

11:33.359 --> 11:35.862
It's not like I drank last night,

11:36.362 --> 11:37.822
but I don't remember a thing.

11:38.990 --> 11:40.533
Are you sure you're okay?

11:40.617 --> 11:41.784
Don't even ask.

11:41.868 --> 11:44.621
Maybe it was all the stress
from getting the press to bury the story

11:44.704 --> 11:46.831
of you beating someone up last week.

11:46.915 --> 11:48.917
Man, I totally blacked out.

11:50.877 --> 11:52.462
Is it morning already?

11:52.545 --> 11:55.006
Today's the call-up
for the international match!

11:56.382 --> 11:58.718
- International match?
- Man, what time is it?

11:59.344 --> 12:00.595
We've got to get ready fast.

12:00.678 --> 12:02.639
Go wash up. I'll pack your bags.

12:36.297 --> 12:39.008
Let's start with some stretching.

12:39.676 --> 12:41.970
- Stretching?
- Like this.

12:43.805 --> 12:45.682
Keep your feet straight.

12:45.765 --> 12:46.933
- Okay.
- Good job.

12:47.016 --> 12:49.519
- Now go down. Reach.
- Okay.

12:52.855 --> 12:55.108
Wait, is that it?

12:55.191 --> 12:56.276
Yeah.

12:56.985 --> 12:58.778
What? Surely not.

12:58.861 --> 13:01.364
Let's try again. There's no way
a human body can be that stiff.

13:01.447 --> 13:02.573
What?

13:03.116 --> 13:04.909
Now, breathe out.

13:10.540 --> 13:12.917
- I can't go any lower.
- That's really it?

13:14.669 --> 13:16.296
- Something's wrong with you.
- What?

13:16.379 --> 13:18.256
Okay, breathe out.

13:18.339 --> 13:19.966
Exhale.

13:20.466 --> 13:21.884
See? You can go lower.

13:21.968 --> 13:24.095
One, two, three, four.

13:24.178 --> 13:25.805
Breathe out.

13:25.888 --> 13:27.849
- Exhale.
- I am!

13:27.932 --> 13:30.643
Now, the sides. The other side.

13:30.727 --> 13:31.894
Exhale.

13:32.895 --> 13:34.230
Let go, Si-yeol.

13:34.314 --> 13:36.316
- Let go!
- You're fine.

13:36.399 --> 13:38.234
I'm telling you, I'm not!

13:38.318 --> 13:41.321
- Stretch!
- I'm going to kill you!

13:41.404 --> 13:43.323
Good job.

13:44.782 --> 13:46.326
- Done resting?
- What?

13:47.201 --> 13:48.745
- Now, exhale.
- Exhale.

13:48.828 --> 13:51.372
- Exhale.
- Exhale!

13:53.249 --> 13:56.794
Si-yeol, I think I'm done.

13:56.878 --> 13:59.339
- What?
- I'm done exercising for today.

14:00.214 --> 14:03.468
What are you talking about?
We only just finished stretching.

14:05.261 --> 14:06.346
Let's run a bit.

14:06.429 --> 14:07.764
No. You go.

14:07.847 --> 14:09.932
I'm going to rest here for a bit.

14:10.016 --> 14:11.642
Running just makes you sweaty.

14:13.269 --> 14:15.563
That's exactly why you run.

14:18.149 --> 14:20.818
Look at them running.
Don't they look cool?

14:21.861 --> 14:23.488
Running will make you feel great.

14:26.491 --> 14:29.327
Okay, one, two, one, two, one.

14:30.536 --> 14:33.539
Si-yeol, how far do we have to run?

14:33.623 --> 14:37.668
Let's run just up to there.
Come on, you can do it!

14:38.836 --> 14:41.714
You got this. Let's go!

14:42.215 --> 14:43.549
That's it.

14:48.805 --> 14:50.932
Why on earth do humans do this

14:51.015 --> 14:53.059
instead of using perfectly good cars?

14:54.852 --> 14:56.729
Isn't this self-torture?

15:01.609 --> 15:02.777
Here.

15:08.616 --> 15:10.243
The water tastes so good, right?

15:10.743 --> 15:12.662
Yeah, I feel much better.

15:12.745 --> 15:13.704
And the breeze is cool.

15:13.788 --> 15:14.789
Doesn't it feel good?

15:20.503 --> 15:22.130
I guess.

15:22.630 --> 15:24.132
You did great.

15:25.049 --> 15:27.468
I thought you'd quit halfway,
but you stuck with it.

15:28.261 --> 15:29.470
This is nothing.

15:33.057 --> 15:34.100
Man, it's hot.

15:35.017 --> 15:38.187
You'll catch a cold
if you take that off now.

16:06.466 --> 16:07.592
There.

16:11.095 --> 16:14.140
We're already warmed up.
Do you want to do a bit more?

16:15.141 --> 16:16.392
What?

16:19.061 --> 16:21.063
Wait. Run more?

16:21.772 --> 16:22.982
No.

16:24.275 --> 16:26.068
Let's go play some soccer.

16:28.571 --> 16:30.781
- Do you want to make a bet?
- A bet?

16:31.324 --> 16:34.452
If you can take this ball from me,
I'll grant you a wish.

16:34.535 --> 16:36.579
- For real?
- Of course.

16:37.497 --> 16:40.124
How hard could it be
to take the ball from you?

16:40.208 --> 16:43.377
Anything I want, right? No take-backs.

16:44.462 --> 16:45.713
Are you even trying?

16:46.881 --> 16:47.798
Just you wait.

16:51.052 --> 16:52.512
Whoa, easy with the hands.

16:57.642 --> 16:58.768
Hey.

17:00.394 --> 17:01.687
Wait.

17:14.951 --> 17:16.953
Hey, that's a foul!

17:17.036 --> 17:18.913
How is that a foul?

17:19.789 --> 17:21.040
Here.

17:22.208 --> 17:24.460
Ok-sun, try harder.
Are you giving up already?

17:25.086 --> 17:26.921
You're wearing knee pads, right?

17:27.004 --> 17:28.089
What?

17:30.424 --> 17:32.385
- Yes!
- Hey, that's a foul.

17:32.468 --> 17:34.804
That was really a foul.

17:54.282 --> 17:56.701
- I won, right?
- What?

17:57.910 --> 18:00.621
Why are you staring at me?
Is there something on my face?

18:01.455 --> 18:03.374
No, it's nothing.

18:07.503 --> 18:10.214
Want to go again?
It's fun now that I took it from you.

18:10.298 --> 18:13.134
Let's do it. No fouls this time.

18:13.217 --> 18:14.343
You too.

18:15.845 --> 18:19.724
Hey, wait. I said no fouls.

18:24.645 --> 18:26.230
What should I wish for?

18:26.314 --> 18:29.567
I've only ever granted wishes.
I've never made one myself,

18:29.650 --> 18:31.319
so I don't know what to ask for.

18:31.402 --> 18:33.446
Hey, I told you that was a foul.

18:33.529 --> 18:36.324
Says who?
You didn't say that at the start.

18:36.407 --> 18:39.577
Do I really have to explain
that kicking someone's shins is a foul?

18:39.660 --> 18:41.912
Don't be petty. Just admit I won.

18:41.996 --> 18:45.875
You're a pro. Do you really have to try
that hard to beat a regular person?

18:47.043 --> 18:49.587
Jeez, you always have a comeback.

18:50.713 --> 18:52.757
Fine, let's just say you won.

18:53.299 --> 18:54.425
Yes!

19:03.392 --> 19:04.852
- Give me your hand.
- What?

19:06.187 --> 19:08.564
We're on a date right now.

19:08.648 --> 19:10.900
I just want to hold hands while we walk.

19:42.139 --> 19:46.644
So,
what should we do when we get home?

19:46.727 --> 19:51.440
Actually, I'm not going home.
I've got to go train right away.

19:52.233 --> 19:55.611
What do you mean?
We've been working out this whole time.

19:55.695 --> 19:59.281
That was just my own workout.
Now I have to train with the team.

19:59.365 --> 20:02.618
Why bother?
It won't matter once we go back.

20:02.702 --> 20:04.161
I have to make money.

20:04.704 --> 20:07.498
They said I need to win matches
to get paid a decent amount.

20:08.582 --> 20:11.127
Plus, we don't have much to do right now.

20:11.210 --> 20:15.256
Don't we have to wait until that chairman
actually hands over the building?

20:15.756 --> 20:18.050
Well, yeah.

20:18.801 --> 20:22.179
After I get my win bonus
from this weekend's match,

20:22.263 --> 20:25.516
I'll treat you to something nice.
Something better than pork cutlets.

20:29.061 --> 20:30.146
No, wait.

20:31.063 --> 20:33.441
Eun-ho, should we go on a trip?

20:34.316 --> 20:36.068
A trip? Just like that?

20:36.152 --> 20:40.740
Well, the match this weekend
is in Suncheon.

20:41.365 --> 20:43.409
I heard the reed fields are nice there.

20:43.492 --> 20:48.873
We could go together, look around,
and get something nice to eat.

20:48.956 --> 20:50.124
How about it?

20:50.750 --> 20:52.418
Sure, whatever.

20:53.085 --> 20:54.420
That's a promise.

20:55.296 --> 20:57.715
Then, you should go home and rest.

20:57.798 --> 20:59.884
You must be tired from all that exercise.

21:00.551 --> 21:03.387
Actually, I just remembered
I have something to do today.

21:03.888 --> 21:04.930
What is it?

21:05.014 --> 21:08.851
We need money for the trip.
I'll make some while you train.

21:08.934 --> 21:10.770
- You?
- I told you.

21:10.853 --> 21:12.980
You should just focus on soccer

21:13.063 --> 21:14.940
because I'll bring home tons of money.

21:21.614 --> 21:22.948
INTERNATIONAL SOCCER

21:29.079 --> 21:31.415
- Hello, sir.
- Hello!

21:31.499 --> 21:33.876
- Congratulations. We love you.
- Congratulations.

21:34.877 --> 21:37.922
Mr. Hyeon,
congratulations on the transfer.

21:38.005 --> 21:40.007
Are you settling in okay?

21:40.090 --> 21:41.050
Pardon?

21:41.133 --> 21:43.177
I mean, since you've transferred.

21:43.260 --> 21:44.261
I see.

21:44.762 --> 21:47.598
Well, I'm still settling in.

21:48.224 --> 21:50.643
Why are you so nervous? It's not like you.

21:50.726 --> 21:51.727
Woo-seok.

21:52.686 --> 21:53.938
How have you been?

21:54.897 --> 21:57.233
- Yeah.
- Congratulations on the transfer, man.

21:57.983 --> 22:00.319
Why are you only filming Woo-seok?
Get me too.

22:00.402 --> 22:02.321
Come on, he's world-class.

22:02.404 --> 22:03.364
Man, that's harsh.

22:04.323 --> 22:06.742
Hey, why haven't you been
answering my DMs?

22:07.576 --> 22:09.912
You mean… I haven't been?

22:10.412 --> 22:13.165
Look at him, acting all distant.

22:13.249 --> 22:15.125
This is how people change
when they make it big.

22:15.209 --> 22:17.086
You need to get this on camera.

22:17.169 --> 22:18.295
Woo-seok!

22:18.379 --> 22:19.630
- Hello.
- Hello.

22:20.130 --> 22:21.882
- Hello.
- Am I invisible to you guys?

22:21.966 --> 22:24.635
Woo-seok was just so blinding.
I didn't even see you.

22:24.718 --> 22:26.053
Good to see you.

22:26.971 --> 22:28.639
- How have you been?
- Good.

22:28.722 --> 22:30.182
Woo-seok, I'll see you later.

22:33.519 --> 22:35.354
We're always rooting for you.

22:35.437 --> 22:36.438
Thanks.

22:49.285 --> 22:51.203
COOKING, FOOD SERVICE

22:51.579 --> 22:53.163
STORE MANAGEMENT, SALES

22:53.789 --> 22:58.586
Let's see. What should I do to make money?

23:00.504 --> 23:03.132
Oh, this hourly pay isn't bad.

23:03.215 --> 23:05.301
Do you have a problem with my resume?

23:06.760 --> 23:07.636
Education?

23:07.720 --> 23:08.929
OFFICE WORK, SALES, EDUCATION

23:09.013 --> 23:12.308
It's Yukyeong Gongwon, the Royal College.

23:12.391 --> 23:15.269
It was Korea's first
modern educational institution.

23:15.352 --> 23:16.687
You've never heard of it?

23:18.063 --> 23:21.233
Not Sungkyunkwan University.
Seonggyungwan National Academy.

23:21.317 --> 23:23.569
Seonggyungwan never handed out diplomas.

23:24.653 --> 23:27.239
Certifications? Look, even without them,

23:27.323 --> 23:30.284
there's nothing I can't do
or haven't done--

23:30.367 --> 23:32.244
Hello?

23:39.293 --> 23:43.255
Why are they so picky
about hiring just a part-timer?

23:46.008 --> 23:48.135
OH SEASON GROCERY STORE NOW HIRING

23:49.219 --> 23:50.804
"No qualifications required."

23:50.888 --> 23:54.266
"No experience required,
and no age limit"?

24:02.733 --> 24:06.070
What the heck?
Why isn't anyone here?

24:09.573 --> 24:10.950
Push up a little more.

24:14.536 --> 24:15.704
SI-YEOL

24:16.330 --> 24:17.539
Where are you?

24:20.459 --> 24:22.378
Jeez. Hello?

24:22.461 --> 24:24.630
- Hey, where are you guys?
- Hey, Si-yeol.

24:24.713 --> 24:26.966
Why aren't you here?
Isn't it training time?

24:27.049 --> 24:29.677
What are you talking about?
Training was canceled.

24:29.760 --> 24:31.720
You didn't get the message earlier?

24:32.346 --> 24:34.056
Tell Si-yeol to come.

24:34.139 --> 24:37.267
Hey, you want to join us?
We're at the internet cafe out front.

24:37.351 --> 24:41.271
We have a match this weekend.
Why did they cancel training?

24:42.022 --> 24:44.024
Never mind. Just get over here.

24:44.108 --> 24:45.526
Let's train by ourselves.

24:45.609 --> 24:47.820
Hello… Hello?

24:47.903 --> 24:49.196
- Hel…
- Don't you dare--

24:49.279 --> 24:50.739
Man, I can't hear a thing.

24:52.116 --> 24:54.201
Man, he's exhausting.

24:54.702 --> 24:57.538
- Why?
- He wants us to come and train on our own.

24:57.621 --> 25:00.791
Jeez, just hearing that makes me tired.

25:00.874 --> 25:03.127
I could go for an iced Americano.

25:03.877 --> 25:06.547
Iced Americano? It's freezing out.

25:07.172 --> 25:09.383
Have this instead.

25:11.051 --> 25:12.553
Quick, give me one.

25:26.400 --> 25:27.693
I feel awake now.

25:29.737 --> 25:30.738
It's good.

25:38.704 --> 25:42.583
I feel like someone's been watching me
from behind for a while now.

25:42.666 --> 25:43.917
What?

25:47.713 --> 25:51.175
Don't you guys feel anything weird?

25:51.258 --> 25:56.096
You know, like someone's
keeping an eye on us.

25:56.597 --> 25:58.182
Who would be looking at us?

25:58.724 --> 26:02.019
Come on, you're not that famous.
Don't be so full of yourself.

26:02.644 --> 26:05.022
- You think so?
- Beom, our base is getting wrecked!

26:05.105 --> 26:06.940
Oh, shoot! What the… Hey!

26:07.024 --> 26:08.734
- Hey.
- Man.

26:08.817 --> 26:09.985
I did warn you.

26:10.569 --> 26:13.822
OH SEASON GROCERY STORE

26:13.906 --> 26:15.491
STANDARD EMPLOYMENT CONTRACT
EUN-HO

26:22.998 --> 26:25.417
So, what's your name?

26:26.335 --> 26:27.628
Eun-ho.

26:28.837 --> 26:30.255
RESIDENT REGISTRATION CARD
KIM OK-SUN

26:31.465 --> 26:32.466
EUN-HO

26:33.592 --> 26:34.843
It doesn't say that here.

26:37.930 --> 26:41.141
Ms. Kim Ok-sun,
this is an employment contract.

26:41.225 --> 26:43.018
You have to write your real name.

26:43.102 --> 26:46.313
How many times do I have to say it?
That's the fake name.

26:46.396 --> 26:48.357
Eun-ho is my real name.

26:52.277 --> 26:53.529
EUN-HO

26:54.363 --> 26:56.198
KIM OK-SUN

26:58.242 --> 27:01.954
You know, Ms. Kim Ok-sun,
you're being a little too casual.

27:03.664 --> 27:05.958
- What?
- Stop speaking informally to me.

27:06.458 --> 27:08.502
What are you good at, Ms. Ok-sun?

27:08.585 --> 27:10.879
You were speaking informally too just now.

27:10.963 --> 27:12.047
Excuse me?

27:12.840 --> 27:14.591
Nothing. Fine.

27:15.217 --> 27:17.469
It won't be easy,
but I'll take it as a unique experience.

27:17.553 --> 27:21.098
I'm good at everything.
There really isn't anything I can't do.

27:21.723 --> 27:23.892
Oh, really? We've got an ace here.

27:23.976 --> 27:25.477
Do you like plushies?

27:29.356 --> 27:31.108
Oh my. How cute.

27:39.867 --> 27:41.785
Why'd you take that? Throw it away.

27:41.869 --> 27:42.953
Damn it.

27:48.333 --> 27:49.751
Seriously?

27:55.883 --> 27:57.342
I don't want it.

27:59.052 --> 28:01.180
Hey, you!

28:06.018 --> 28:07.561
- Wow!
- What's that?

28:07.644 --> 28:10.814
Stay back! Don't come here. Go away!

28:10.898 --> 28:13.150
Hey, stop! It'll come off!

28:24.286 --> 28:25.662
DAEHEUNG CITIZENS FC

28:31.043 --> 28:33.879
Oh gosh, sir…

28:35.339 --> 28:36.298
Why are you here?

28:36.381 --> 28:39.343
Coach, I knocked a bunch of times.

28:43.096 --> 28:44.014
What do you want?

28:44.097 --> 28:45.641
Is today's training really canceled?

28:49.102 --> 28:51.939
Yeah. Didn't you get the message?

28:52.022 --> 28:55.609
What we need is more practice,
so how could you…

28:55.692 --> 28:56.818
Man.

28:58.612 --> 29:00.906
Wait. What is that smell?

29:07.246 --> 29:08.705
Coach, were you drinking?

29:09.289 --> 29:11.500
The match is right around the corner,

29:11.583 --> 29:13.418
but you canceled practice, and now this?

29:13.502 --> 29:15.379
Gosh, I'm hungover.

29:17.464 --> 29:18.882
Si-yeol, did you eat yet?

29:19.967 --> 29:21.051
Pardon?

29:21.593 --> 29:22.719
Let's go grab a bite.

29:24.638 --> 29:25.597
Gosh.

29:43.699 --> 29:46.493
- What is this?
- It's totally burnt.

29:47.202 --> 29:48.704
You expect us to eat this?

29:49.329 --> 29:51.832
Should I throw it away then?
That's wasteful.

29:53.166 --> 29:54.334
Man, I burnt another one.

29:55.210 --> 29:57.045
It's because you kept talking to me.

29:57.129 --> 29:59.423
Just eat and move along.

30:03.260 --> 30:04.594
I'm not buying this.

30:14.438 --> 30:16.064
Maybe this is a bit too burnt.

30:18.442 --> 30:20.902
Don't cause trouble this time.

30:20.986 --> 30:23.030
Got it, Ms. Kim Ok-sun?

30:23.113 --> 30:24.698
This is much better.

30:24.781 --> 30:28.368
They should've put me
on this from the start.

30:38.211 --> 30:40.464
Come over here! I'll ring you up.

31:08.325 --> 31:09.493
What?

31:13.955 --> 31:15.957
I don't think the discount was applied.

31:17.125 --> 31:19.002
- What?
- Look, right here.

31:19.086 --> 31:21.046
You need to ring it up again.

31:22.756 --> 31:23.757
Jeez.

31:30.055 --> 31:31.640
CHECK RECEIPT, CHECK PRICE

31:34.893 --> 31:36.353
Cancel…

31:43.068 --> 31:46.822
Look, I don't know how to cancel this.

31:46.905 --> 31:48.990
- Can't we just let it slide?
- Excuse me?

31:49.074 --> 31:53.120
Also, I like being cashier,
so don't file a complaint.

31:53.203 --> 31:55.205
- Let's keep this between us.
- That's ridiculous--

31:55.288 --> 31:57.207
Just consider the 1,750 won as a donation.

31:59.543 --> 32:01.044
It'll bring you good luck.

32:18.854 --> 32:21.481
I knew it was going too smoothly.

32:21.565 --> 32:23.275
Gosh, this is chaos.

32:23.775 --> 32:26.236
Maybe I should've just let them complain.

32:28.905 --> 32:30.240
Excuse me.

32:32.075 --> 32:33.493
A check?

32:35.036 --> 32:36.455
You don't have cash or a card?

32:36.538 --> 32:38.540
Why? Is there a problem?

32:40.459 --> 32:43.003
Just use a card.
I don't know how to process that.

32:43.086 --> 32:46.381
If you have a problem with that,
you should file a complaint.

32:46.465 --> 32:48.008
- Excuse me?
- A complaint.

32:48.091 --> 32:49.801
Ma'am, let me help you with that.

32:52.137 --> 32:54.764
Just press this, and then this for checks.

32:54.848 --> 32:57.851
Get a signature on the back
and give her the change.

32:58.602 --> 33:00.562
Okay. Thanks.

33:04.274 --> 33:05.484
Sorry about that.

33:17.454 --> 33:18.872
You're not drinking, right?

33:19.706 --> 33:20.790
No.

33:26.546 --> 33:27.923
Gosh.

33:28.548 --> 33:31.635
Who drinks soju like it's water?

33:37.474 --> 33:38.975
What's going on?

33:40.393 --> 33:41.561
Hey, Si-yeol.

33:44.064 --> 33:45.065
We're done for.

33:46.316 --> 33:48.109
What do you mean?

33:48.985 --> 33:52.447
I'm talking about our team, you punk.

33:52.531 --> 33:54.908
Come on, Coach.

33:55.742 --> 33:58.286
We're last in the fourth division.
We can't get any lower.

33:58.370 --> 34:01.164
How can we be "done for"?

34:01.915 --> 34:03.708
I told you, I'll get us promoted.

34:03.792 --> 34:06.336
Promotion doesn't even matter.

34:08.421 --> 34:09.506
You know

34:10.465 --> 34:12.842
the director who sponsors us, right?

34:13.552 --> 34:15.679
The director at my grandma's nursing home?

34:16.346 --> 34:17.264
Yes, him.

34:17.847 --> 34:19.224
Well, that director said

34:20.392 --> 34:23.144
he can't sponsor us anymore.

34:24.646 --> 34:25.605
What?

34:26.439 --> 34:29.150
A sponsorship contract isn't a joke.

34:29.234 --> 34:30.652
He can't just break it overnight.

34:30.735 --> 34:34.698
Well, what else can we do?

34:35.490 --> 34:39.202
Like you said,
we're in the fourth division.

34:39.953 --> 34:44.874
It's not exactly good publicity
to sponsor the last-place team.

34:44.958 --> 34:47.419
The director
was just sponsoring us for years

34:47.961 --> 34:52.048
as a service to the community
because he liked soccer.

34:52.799 --> 34:56.219
But he said he can't afford it anymore,
so there's nothing we can do.

35:02.392 --> 35:03.435
Then,

35:04.728 --> 35:05.979
what do we do now?

35:07.689 --> 35:09.441
What happens to the team?

35:09.524 --> 35:11.818
We have to find a new sponsor.

35:12.444 --> 35:13.945
It won't be easy, though.

35:15.196 --> 35:17.198
We're not going down like this.

35:17.282 --> 35:19.409
No, I mean

35:19.492 --> 35:21.620
what happens if we don't find one?

35:21.703 --> 35:23.371
What do you think, you punk?

35:23.455 --> 35:27.375
The club goes bankrupt,
and the team disbands.

35:36.676 --> 35:38.345
Forget about paying the players.

35:40.430 --> 35:43.266
We can't even pay the rent
for the training ground.

35:44.392 --> 35:45.810
What can we do?

35:51.775 --> 35:54.486
Don't tell the other guys, okay?

35:56.696 --> 35:58.823
I shouldn't have even told you.

36:00.408 --> 36:03.828
I just had to get it off my chest.

36:16.466 --> 36:18.218
I've been thinking.

36:19.427 --> 36:22.931
I don't think
you're a good fit for our store.

36:23.014 --> 36:25.767
I'll pay you for your work today,

36:26.309 --> 36:28.144
but you don't need to come in anymore.

36:28.228 --> 36:30.021
Really? That's fine.

36:30.980 --> 36:34.818
The pay was too low
for the workload anyway.

36:42.033 --> 36:43.326
I'm sorry to bother you,

36:43.410 --> 36:45.620
but the totals aren't adding up.

36:46.454 --> 36:47.956
What?

36:48.039 --> 36:49.999
Ms. Kim's cash drawer is off.

37:10.437 --> 37:11.688
What did I just do?

37:12.313 --> 37:16.568
You gave the customer back
her 100,000-won check and the change.

37:17.694 --> 37:20.238
That explains
why we're exactly 100,000 won short.

37:20.947 --> 37:24.451
So, what happens to me?

37:24.534 --> 37:26.077
It's okay.

37:26.161 --> 37:29.748
Mistakes happen. Don't worry about it.

37:30.415 --> 37:31.458
Really?

37:32.876 --> 37:34.252
Of course.

37:34.335 --> 37:36.755
Just pay it back. No big deal.

37:37.630 --> 37:38.757
What?

37:38.840 --> 37:41.634
Your hourly pay is 10,030 won,

37:41.718 --> 37:45.096
and you worked for five hours,
so that's 50,150 won for today.

37:45.180 --> 37:48.224
But with the 100,000 won loss,

37:50.101 --> 37:53.438
you just owe us 49,850 won.

37:54.898 --> 37:56.065
Owe you?

37:56.775 --> 38:01.571
You mean you're not even paying me,

38:01.654 --> 38:04.699
but I have to pay you 49,850 won?

38:04.783 --> 38:07.076
I worked like a dog
all day for this place!

38:07.744 --> 38:09.037
That's too bad.

38:13.041 --> 38:15.376
I walked here just to save bus fare!

38:16.169 --> 38:18.046
Can't you let this slide?

38:19.631 --> 38:22.467
I can't do that.
I'm just an employee here.

38:41.903 --> 38:45.114
I bragged about bringing home money.

38:45.198 --> 38:46.866
What do I tell Si-yeol?

38:47.867 --> 38:51.246
I can't say I worked all day
just to end up in debt.

38:55.458 --> 38:57.502
Should I sell the clothes?

39:10.974 --> 39:13.059
- Si-yeol, you're home!
- Yeah.

39:14.519 --> 39:16.437
- What's wrong?
- What?

39:17.188 --> 39:20.775
I mean, you went to training,
and you're back looking so dejected again.

39:21.317 --> 39:23.611
Well, that's…

39:28.825 --> 39:31.077
It's nothing.
The team's just having some issues.

39:32.579 --> 39:35.039
Si-yeol, want me to cheer you up?

39:35.665 --> 39:36.708
All of a sudden?

39:37.542 --> 39:39.294
Here. I made some money.

39:42.046 --> 39:45.425
Wow, it's pretty thick.

39:48.052 --> 39:51.431
- How much is this?
- It's 200,000 won. I did good, right?

39:52.724 --> 39:55.894
Wait, what did you do
to get 200,000 won in a day?

39:58.021 --> 39:59.939
You didn't steal this, did you?

40:01.858 --> 40:03.943
I'm on a mission
to do good deeds right now.

40:04.027 --> 40:07.488
How can you say that
to someone who's trying to live right?

40:07.572 --> 40:09.782
I know. You're right.

40:10.283 --> 40:12.035
But where did you earn this much in a--

40:12.118 --> 40:14.996
I've got skills.
I've been around the block, you know.

40:15.705 --> 40:17.707
The details are a trade secret.

40:18.333 --> 40:21.210
You haven't eaten yet, right?
Let's go out. It's my treat.

40:25.924 --> 40:28.301
I told you to fix your doorbell already.

40:28.384 --> 40:30.678
- Oh, hello.
- Hello.

40:31.346 --> 40:33.348
What are you guys doing here?

40:35.016 --> 40:38.102
Did you guys hear something?

40:38.978 --> 40:39.896
Hear what?

40:40.521 --> 40:42.690
The international match is today.

40:42.774 --> 40:44.025
We came to watch it together.

40:44.108 --> 40:45.735
Hello, Eun-ho.

41:03.878 --> 41:04.837
Hey!

41:11.302 --> 41:13.972
Eun-ho, you haven't tried
my family's galbi, right?

41:14.055 --> 41:16.182
Jeong-bae's folks
bought a building selling this galbi.

41:16.265 --> 41:17.350
It's good.

41:17.433 --> 41:19.852
Really? I haven't had beef galbi
in a while.

41:21.604 --> 41:24.857
Why couldn't you guys
just watch the game at home?

41:24.941 --> 41:26.943
Come on, don't be like that.

41:27.026 --> 41:29.696
We always watch
the international games here together.

41:30.238 --> 41:32.281
Aren't you glad we're here, Eun-ho?

41:33.616 --> 41:36.577
Of course. Beef galbi is always welcome.

41:37.662 --> 41:39.539
- Let's eat.
- Let's eat.

41:39.622 --> 41:42.291
How can you call yourself an athlete
when you're drinking this late?

41:42.375 --> 41:44.711
Again with the nagging.

41:44.794 --> 41:47.213
You don't have to drink.

41:47.296 --> 41:51.259
Today's a good day,
so how about just one, okay?

41:52.010 --> 41:53.886
Would you like a glass, Eun-ho?

41:53.970 --> 41:55.138
Sure, pour me one.

41:58.766 --> 42:01.227
Okay, fine.

42:01.310 --> 42:04.188
What's the point of nagging
you guys anyway?

42:04.272 --> 42:05.481
Just don't overdo it.

42:06.232 --> 42:07.567
Okay!

42:07.650 --> 42:10.028
Nice seeing you again, Eun-ho.

42:10.111 --> 42:12.447
- Nice to see you!
- Cheers!

42:25.001 --> 42:27.211
You know, it's really weird.

42:28.046 --> 42:29.047
What is?

42:30.381 --> 42:32.800
Actually, since yesterday…

42:32.884 --> 42:35.887
Man, it's getting chilly.
I might catch a cold.

42:40.433 --> 42:42.518
They must've fixed the streetlight.

42:42.602 --> 42:44.145
It had been left broken for months.

42:50.651 --> 42:51.694
What the…

42:52.695 --> 42:53.696
Who is it?

43:05.416 --> 43:06.876
You were stalked?

43:07.376 --> 43:09.587
Who'd stalk you?

43:09.670 --> 43:12.381
I know how crazy it sounds--

43:12.465 --> 43:15.051
Beom, were you up all night gaming again?

43:15.134 --> 43:17.220
It's because you're tired, that's all.

43:17.303 --> 43:19.305
See? You've got dark circles
under your eyes.

43:19.388 --> 43:20.807
That's…

43:21.933 --> 43:23.935
just because I'm stressed out.

43:24.018 --> 43:26.062
Why are you stressed?

43:26.145 --> 43:27.855
Bet his stocks tanked again.

43:27.939 --> 43:30.858
How's that my fault?
The domestic market is a total mess.

43:31.567 --> 43:35.404
I thought Si-yeol was the only one broke,
but you're penniless too, aren't you?

43:35.488 --> 43:37.990
Come on, I'm different from Si-yeol.

43:38.074 --> 43:39.700
He's all about soccer without a plan,

43:39.784 --> 43:42.995
and I ended up like this
trying to prepare for the future.

43:45.832 --> 43:46.958
What is it?

43:48.793 --> 43:50.294
What was that just now?

43:50.920 --> 43:54.215
Something flashed. Was it lightning?

43:54.841 --> 43:56.342
But the sky is clear.

44:03.975 --> 44:05.268
Si-yeol.

44:06.102 --> 44:07.311
Come out for a second.

44:11.899 --> 44:14.694
What's the matter all of a sudden?

44:16.112 --> 44:19.031
Come out. How long are you going to hide?

44:19.115 --> 44:20.533
What?

44:24.495 --> 44:25.788
Hello, sis.

44:43.014 --> 44:45.391
- It's me, Secretary Choi.
- Come in.

44:55.401 --> 44:56.485
Hey.

44:56.569 --> 44:59.197
Congratulations on returning home, sir.

45:01.741 --> 45:05.745
Honestly, I've always hated this place
because my old man was here.

45:05.828 --> 45:07.288
It was more fun out there.

45:08.748 --> 45:12.877
But you know, after wandering around,

45:12.960 --> 45:14.337
there really is no place like home.

45:14.420 --> 45:17.840
After ten years,
it was even nice to see my father.

45:19.175 --> 45:20.635
Are you back for good now, sir?

45:24.263 --> 45:27.350
Of course. No need for me to run anymore.

45:28.684 --> 45:31.771
Anyway, what's that damn shaman up to?

45:36.484 --> 45:40.738
He's searching every
antique shop and bookstore in the country.

45:40.821 --> 45:42.740
Seems like he's looking for something.

45:44.325 --> 45:47.954
He told me to wait and do nothing,
but what the hell is he doing?

45:48.037 --> 45:50.748
I need him to catch that other fox

45:51.415 --> 45:53.834
so I can get on with my business, damn it.

45:54.543 --> 45:57.880
Also, the fourth-division soccer matter
is proceeding as you've requested.

45:57.964 --> 45:59.966
Oh, really?

46:00.633 --> 46:02.176
How are you proceeding with it?

46:04.178 --> 46:06.722
I found corruption and nepotism
at the sponsoring nursing home

46:06.806 --> 46:08.599
tied to its founding family.

46:08.683 --> 46:11.310
I told them to choose
between the whole family going to jail

46:11.394 --> 46:12.645
or ending the sponsorship.

46:13.271 --> 46:16.148
They should've announced
the termination of the sponsorship by now.

46:16.232 --> 46:17.525
Good job.

46:19.193 --> 46:21.404
How did you know I was here?

46:21.487 --> 46:24.073
That light earlier.
You gained spiritual power, didn't you?

46:25.574 --> 46:27.326
- Really?
- Yeah.

46:27.410 --> 46:29.829
Yes, I did.
I got a huge amount of spiritual power.

46:29.912 --> 46:33.582
A few more times like this,
and I'll have nine tails in no time.

46:33.666 --> 46:37.003
That old man, Chairman Kim, worked fast.

46:39.839 --> 46:42.591
Anyway, why were you hiding there?

46:42.675 --> 46:45.094
You could've just said you were here.

46:46.595 --> 46:47.638
Pardon?

46:48.222 --> 46:49.640
Was it because of the guys inside?

46:49.724 --> 46:51.767
Since when did she have that kind of tact?

46:51.851 --> 46:53.352
How long have you been there?

46:54.103 --> 46:56.731
Well, since the beginning?

46:59.859 --> 47:01.652
You're acting suspicious.

47:05.448 --> 47:06.449
Hold on.

47:07.950 --> 47:11.162
You weren't here for us, were you?

47:13.831 --> 47:17.376
Don't tell me you're the one
stalking that stock junkie?

47:33.351 --> 47:34.268
Yes.

47:35.269 --> 47:36.312
What?

47:41.525 --> 47:43.402
Man, we're out of sauce.

47:44.111 --> 47:46.364
Our beef galbi is already seasoned.

47:46.447 --> 47:48.157
It tastes better just as it is.

47:49.033 --> 47:51.827
No, I like the sauce. I'll go buy some.

47:51.911 --> 47:53.454
Are you crazy?

47:59.126 --> 48:01.754
I should just eat it as is, right?

48:01.837 --> 48:04.090
I was wondering if we did something wrong,

48:04.173 --> 48:05.841
but I guess
it was Si-yeol who messed up.

48:05.925 --> 48:07.843
It's not good to get involved
in a couple's fight.

48:07.927 --> 48:09.762
Maybe we should've left earlier.

48:09.845 --> 48:12.014
Well, it's not too late.

48:12.765 --> 48:15.684
You want to go past them
while they're going at each other?

48:15.768 --> 48:17.561
I don't think that's a good idea.

48:18.354 --> 48:21.190
- We're totally trapped here.
- Yeah.

48:24.485 --> 48:26.737
Just turn on the TV.
The match is about to start anyway.

48:26.821 --> 48:27.822
- Okay.
- Shall we?

48:27.905 --> 48:28.948
Yeah.

48:29.615 --> 48:30.699
Wait.

48:31.367 --> 48:33.077
Where did that go?

48:36.414 --> 48:37.415
"That"?

48:37.498 --> 48:40.084
You stupid eight-tailed fox.
Didn't I warn you about humans?

48:40.167 --> 48:42.461
Especially men, of all people?

48:42.545 --> 48:43.838
You didn't!

48:45.256 --> 48:46.632
- I didn't?
- No.

48:47.633 --> 48:49.260
I don't think you said that.

48:50.136 --> 48:52.096
Do I have to spell it out for you?

48:52.179 --> 48:54.473
How would I know if you didn't say it?

48:54.557 --> 48:56.183
Just wait a second!

48:56.725 --> 48:58.310
Please!

49:00.104 --> 49:01.564
Just calm down.

49:01.647 --> 49:03.274
Why should I?

49:03.941 --> 49:08.195
Come on, what is it?
Let's calmly talk about it.

49:08.279 --> 49:10.573
How does blowing up like that
help anything?

49:10.656 --> 49:14.910
You look exactly like her,
and you even act just like her.

49:16.203 --> 49:18.581
Listen to me carefully.

49:18.664 --> 49:20.458
I won't stop you from becoming human.

49:20.541 --> 49:21.792
But men?

49:21.876 --> 49:25.629
Do you know how many women
ruin their lives over men?

49:25.713 --> 49:28.841
- Especially naive girls like you.
- Hey.

49:28.924 --> 49:32.094
Girls like you
need to be extra careful around men.

49:32.178 --> 49:33.345
Then what about you?

49:34.847 --> 49:36.056
What?

49:36.140 --> 49:37.600
I saw everything.

49:37.683 --> 49:39.185
You held hands,

49:39.810 --> 49:42.062
and last night at Namsan…

49:42.146 --> 49:45.608
That's… different.

49:46.108 --> 49:47.109
How so?

49:47.193 --> 49:49.612
I'm going back to how I was, and this guy…

49:53.866 --> 49:55.242
is decent and great at soccer,

49:55.326 --> 49:58.204
despite how he looks now.

50:00.664 --> 50:01.916
But look at you.

50:01.999 --> 50:05.794
You barely know that guy,
so why are you stalking him?

50:05.878 --> 50:07.505
What do you even see in him?

50:07.588 --> 50:08.923
His face.

50:09.715 --> 50:11.550
Come again?

50:14.303 --> 50:15.679
He's good-looking.

50:17.598 --> 50:20.809
See? This is exactly why I'm worried.

50:21.519 --> 50:24.063
Do you think his looks
are going to pay the bills?

50:24.772 --> 50:28.234
Why are you so against this?

50:28.317 --> 50:31.820
Let her like him. She'll learn from it.

50:31.904 --> 50:34.406
You said he's broke, and she's clueless!

50:34.490 --> 50:37.868
He should at least have something
if he's going to take care of that idiot.

50:39.119 --> 50:41.872
Of all the men out there…

50:42.998 --> 50:45.167
Isn't there anyone else?

50:47.711 --> 50:50.422
Sorry to interrupt.

50:50.506 --> 50:52.758
Right. What about him?

50:52.841 --> 50:55.302
At least he isn't broke.

50:55.386 --> 50:56.595
What?

50:57.388 --> 50:59.640
Jeong-bae, what's up?

51:00.266 --> 51:04.895
Well, it's just that
we think you've been robbed.

51:06.397 --> 51:07.481
Robbed?

51:19.660 --> 51:20.536
Weird.

51:22.079 --> 51:23.497
Do thieves these days

51:24.456 --> 51:26.750
steal the AC off the wall?

51:26.834 --> 51:30.129
Jeez, that was the only thing
in this house worth any money.

51:30.212 --> 51:32.464
How did they know to take that?

51:32.548 --> 51:35.134
Si-yeol, is there
anything else you're missing?

51:36.010 --> 51:38.053
I don't know. Eun-ho.

51:39.263 --> 51:40.639
Are you missing anything?

51:41.807 --> 51:43.267
Just out of curiosity…

51:45.728 --> 51:48.105
did that thing double as a heater?

51:49.523 --> 51:50.983
No, not really.

51:51.066 --> 51:53.944
Right? That's a relief.

51:54.820 --> 51:56.405
What's with that reaction?

52:00.951 --> 52:02.703
So, about the AC,

52:03.329 --> 52:04.747
- I sold it.
- What?

52:05.372 --> 52:07.750
We won't be here in the summer anyway.

52:07.833 --> 52:09.710
It's winter and it's freezing.

52:09.793 --> 52:11.920
So it's not like we'll need AC, right?

52:12.796 --> 52:14.798
That's true.

52:15.424 --> 52:18.677
Good job. We're broke anyway.

52:18.761 --> 52:21.263
- So that's where the cash came from?
- Yeah.

52:21.347 --> 52:22.931
Oh, I see.

52:25.517 --> 52:27.770
I guess you sold it.

52:27.853 --> 52:29.813
Well, as long as you weren't robbed.

52:29.897 --> 52:31.607
- Yeah.
- Right.

52:31.690 --> 52:34.485
How much did you get for it, Eun-ho?

52:35.861 --> 52:39.657
- What?
- She gave me 200,000 won.

52:39.740 --> 52:40.824
- What?
- What?

52:40.908 --> 52:42.618
You sold it for 200,000 won?

52:42.701 --> 52:45.412
Why? Was it worth more?

52:45.496 --> 52:48.499
That was the latest model
he bought this summer.

52:49.124 --> 52:50.959
It's worth at least 400,000 won.

52:51.043 --> 52:52.586
At least 400,000?

52:52.670 --> 52:56.465
Wait. What about the outdoor unit?

52:57.257 --> 52:58.884
Did you sell that too?

52:58.967 --> 53:01.512
Yeah, because you don't need it
without the AC.

53:01.595 --> 53:03.597
They said they'd get rid of it for me,

53:03.681 --> 53:05.474
even though
you usually have to pay for that.

53:05.557 --> 53:08.811
The outdoor unit alone
must be worth over 50,000 won.

53:09.478 --> 53:11.188
Maybe even 100,000 won.

53:12.147 --> 53:15.901
Did you say 100,000 won?
People sell those too?

53:17.695 --> 53:19.571
Did I just get scammed?

53:45.889 --> 53:46.974
Hey, are you okay?

53:47.725 --> 53:48.809
What?

53:48.892 --> 53:50.436
Why are you so tense?

53:50.519 --> 53:52.771
It's not your first time
on the national team.

53:54.440 --> 53:58.402
Right. Maybe it's because
I've always dreamed of this.

54:01.029 --> 54:02.865
But my heartbeat feels strange.

54:06.076 --> 54:07.703
What are you talking about?

54:07.786 --> 54:10.539
Don't be nervous. We got this.

54:13.250 --> 54:14.877
Jeez.

54:15.753 --> 54:19.339
Why is everyone drinking booze
like water in front of me today?

54:21.341 --> 54:24.470
If you're going to drink,
at least eat something with it. Okay?

54:25.012 --> 54:26.096
Here.

54:29.308 --> 54:33.353
Why are you so upset? These things happen.

54:33.437 --> 54:34.521
Si-yeol.

54:35.731 --> 54:38.150
Living as a human is just too hard.

54:38.776 --> 54:39.651
What?

54:47.951 --> 54:51.163
Are you crying? You should stop drinking.

54:51.997 --> 54:54.249
I was just trying to do things right.

54:55.250 --> 54:57.711
That's why I took the job at the store.

54:58.337 --> 55:02.758
But they worked me all day,
called me useless, and didn't pay me.

55:03.675 --> 55:07.095
Then they told me to pay back 49,850 won.

55:07.930 --> 55:10.307
What? Which store was that?

55:10.390 --> 55:11.725
Are they insane?

55:12.601 --> 55:16.563
So I tried to fix it
by selling used stuff online,

55:17.481 --> 55:20.150
but I got scammed doing that too.

55:20.651 --> 55:23.570
I really can't live like this anymore.

55:23.654 --> 55:25.781
Come on, Eun-ho.

55:26.615 --> 55:29.701
Eun-ho, it's okay.

55:31.954 --> 55:33.080
It's okay.

55:33.163 --> 55:36.542
You don't have to be here with me.
Go inside and watch the game.

55:37.501 --> 55:40.629
The international match starts soon,
doesn't it?

55:42.422 --> 55:44.007
What's the point of me watching that?

55:44.925 --> 55:49.054
I know Woo-seok is playing instead of me,

55:49.137 --> 55:52.099
but I don't exactly
want to watch it myself.

55:54.268 --> 55:57.771
It's hard for you too, right? I'm sorry.

55:57.855 --> 56:01.066
Eun-ho, I didn't say that to make you cry.

56:01.817 --> 56:02.818
Don't worry.

56:03.944 --> 56:09.032
I promise I'll get you back
to your old life, okay?

56:11.952 --> 56:13.453
I really promise.

56:17.875 --> 56:19.126
What?

56:21.003 --> 56:22.796
We're doing just fine.

56:23.714 --> 56:25.340
Let's not worry too much.

56:53.160 --> 56:54.786
Si-yeol!

56:54.870 --> 56:56.455
Something big happened!

56:56.538 --> 56:57.831
What happened?

56:57.915 --> 57:00.292
Hey, Si-yeol!

57:03.086 --> 57:04.087
Hyeon Woo-seok collapsed!

57:05.005 --> 57:05.881
What?

57:13.138 --> 57:15.098
He collapsed right before the match.

57:30.030 --> 57:31.698
- Woo-seok!
- Hey, Woo-seok!

57:31.782 --> 57:33.450
- Woo-seok!
- Coach!

57:33.533 --> 57:34.952
Apparently, it was cardiac arrest.

57:36.411 --> 57:38.747
They say he might die.

57:41.458 --> 57:42.459
What did you say?

57:49.091 --> 57:50.467
Woo-seok!

57:50.550 --> 57:52.386
Hey, wake up. Come on!

57:53.011 --> 57:54.221
Damn it!

57:59.351 --> 58:01.186
Over here!

58:10.362 --> 58:13.657
Eun-ho, what's happening right now?

58:14.199 --> 58:17.077
- Why is Woo-seok…
- I don't know.

58:17.577 --> 58:19.663
I just switched your fates. That's all.

58:20.288 --> 58:21.623
I'm not sure what's happening.

58:21.707 --> 58:22.624
Wait.

58:24.960 --> 58:28.797
Then, what just happened to Woo-seok

58:30.507 --> 58:33.093
was the fate that was meant for me?

58:36.596 --> 58:39.641
Am I the reason he ended up like this?

58:41.727 --> 58:45.897
Woo-seok might die instead of me?

58:51.486 --> 58:55.449
If that's true, what happens now?

58:57.284 --> 59:01.705
If you go back to normal,
can we reverse all this?

59:04.041 --> 59:05.125
I can't reverse it.

59:07.252 --> 59:08.211
What?

59:08.295 --> 59:09.337
Charging 150 joules.

59:10.630 --> 59:12.591
One, two, clear!

59:13.175 --> 59:15.802
Charging 200 joules. One, two, clear!

59:17.137 --> 59:18.847
I can't reverse it.

59:19.473 --> 59:22.017
If your friend dies in your place,

59:22.100 --> 59:25.312
there's nothing I can do,
even if I'm back to normal.

59:25.937 --> 59:28.356
There's no way for me to reverse your fate

59:28.440 --> 59:30.817
or to bring your friend back.

59:49.211 --> 59:51.129
SPECIAL APPEARANCE BY HONG SU-HYEON

01:00:15.695 --> 01:00:18.615
NO TAIL TO TELL

01:00:18.698 --> 01:00:23.203
Did you think tampering with human fate
was a trivial matter?

01:00:23.286 --> 01:00:24.871
Let's switch back now.

01:00:24.955 --> 01:00:26.957
It's not possible right now.

01:00:27.040 --> 01:00:29.209
Why isn't it possible now?

01:00:29.292 --> 01:00:32.045
You know it too, don't you?
That you're going to die soon.

01:00:32.129 --> 01:00:34.756
I wouldn't sell this
for all the gold in the world.

01:00:34.840 --> 01:00:37.050
- Who are you?
- I didn't expect to find

01:00:37.134 --> 01:00:39.469
another one hiding in a place like this.

01:00:39.553 --> 01:00:43.140
Fix this twisted fate
with your own two hands.

01:00:43.223 --> 01:00:45.934
You want me to just die
instead of Si-yeol?

01:00:46.017 --> 01:00:48.186
So I need you to help me.

01:00:50.561 --> 01:00:52.566
Subtitle translation by Susanna Kim
